{
  "summary": "Enables `-Wunused` and related compiler warning flags in the CMake build configuration. Across 168 files, it silences resulting warnings by removing unused function parameter names, marking necessary unused variables with `[[maybe_unused]]`, and switching static header constants to `inline constexpr`.",
  "problem": "The build system does not enforce `-Wunused`, allowing dead code, unused parameters, and unused variables to accumulate undetected. In some cases, unused code is not actually dead but represents logic mistakenly omitted or forgotten (such as in #36137).",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description notes: 'We've had a handful of dead code removal PRs over the last month or two... Also well as an instance of what was thought to be dead code, but it'd actually just been forgotten to be used: #36137.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": [
      "#36275"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Large mechanical cleanup touching 168 files across the entire codebase. Several commits are marked `[[nomerge]]` because they contain modifications that need to be upstreamed into subtree repositories (minisketch, leveldb, libmultiprocess, crc32c) before this PR can merge.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "This draft RFC enables `-Wunused` compiler warning flags in the build system and cleans up unused parameters and variables across 168 files. Without `-Wunused` enforcement in CI, unused variables and dead code accumulate undetected, which has occasionally masked logic bugs where intended function calls were simply forgotten (such as in #36137). The changes are mostly mechanical, removing unused parameter names or annotating them with `[[maybe_unused]]`. Several commits are placeholders for upstream subtree repositories (Minisketch, LevelDB, libmultiprocess) that must be merged upstream first.",
